      "description": "Authentication endpoints for user registration, login, and token management.\n\n## Multi-tenant Architecture\nAll authentication is multi-tenant aware:\n- JWT tokens contain `orgId` from user's primary organization\n- All subsequent API calls are automatically scoped to that organization\n- Cannot access data from other organizations\n\n## Token Strategy\n- **Access Token**: 15 minute expiry, used for API calls\n- **Refresh Token**: 7 day expiry, used to get new access tokens\n\n## Security\n- Passwords hashed with bcrypt (12 rounds)\n- JWT signed with HS256\n- Global JWT guard protects all endpoints except those marked `@Public()`"
    },
    {
      "name": "WhatsApp Webhooks",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Webhook Verification",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/webhooks/whatsapp?hub.mode=subscribe&hub.verify_token={{webhookVerifyToken}}&hub.challenge=test123",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["webhooks", "whatsapp"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "hub.mode",
                  "value": "subscribe"
                },
                {
                  "key": "hub.verify_token",
                  "value": "{{webhookVerifyToken}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "hub.challenge",
                  "value": "test123"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "WhatsApp webhook verification endpoint.\n\n**Public endpoint** - No authentication required.\n\n### What it does:\nMeta (Facebook) calls this endpoint during webhook setup to verify your server.\n\n### Query Parameters:\n- `hub.mode` - Should be \"subscribe\"\n- `hub.verify_token` - Your verification token (from WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN)\n- `hub.challenge` - Random string sent by Meta\n\n### Response:\nIf verification succeeds, returns the `hub.challenge` value.\n\n### Setup:\n1. Set `webhookVerifyToken` variable to your token\n2. Run this request to test\n3. Use the webhook URL in Meta Business Suite"
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "Success",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/webhooks/whatsapp?hub.mode=subscribe&hub.verify_token=your-webhook-verify-token&hub.challenge=test123",
                  "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["webhooks", "whatsapp"],
                  "query": [
                    {
                      "key": "hub.mode",
                      "value": "subscribe"
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "hub.verify_token",
                      "value": "your-webhook-verify-token"
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "hub.challenge",
                      "value": "test123"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "text",
              "header": [
                {
                  "key": "Content-Type",
                  "value": "text/plain"
                }
